1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,890
Good evening, everyone.

2
00:00:01,890 --> 00:00:05,023
Let me start by welcoming you all to this talk

3
00:00:05,023 --> 00:00:11,550
and thanking you for taking the time to consider joining ACE voluntary organisation.

4
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:16,225
ACE offers support to people and services in the local area

5
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:20,900
and we’re now looking for more volunteers to help us do this.

6
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:26,178
By the way, I hope you’re all comfortable – we have brought in extra seats

7
00:00:26,178 --> 00:00:27,965
so that no one has to stand,

8
00:00:27,965 --> 00:00:31,196
but it does mean that the people at the back of the room may

9
00:00:31,196 --> 00:00:32,400
be a bit squashed.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,725
We’ll only be here for about half an hour so, hopefully,

11
00:00:36,725 --> 00:00:37,690
that’s OK.

12
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:42,694
One of the first questions we’re often asked is how old you need to

13
00:00:42,694 --> 00:00:43,940
be to volunteer.

14
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:48,675
Well, you can be as young as 16 or you can be 60

15
00:00:48,675 --> 00:00:49,136
or over;

16
00:00:49,136 --> 00:00:53,690
it all depends on what type of voluntary work you want to do.

17
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:59,186
Other considerations, such as reliability, are crucial in voluntary work

18
00:00:59,186 --> 00:01:03,820
and age isn’t related to these, in our experience.

19
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:07,930
Another question we get asked relates to training.

20
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:12,880
Well, there’s plenty of that and it’s all face-to-face.

21
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:20,172
What’s more, training doesn’t end when you start working for us – it takes place before, during

22
00:01:20,172 --> 00:01:21,940
and after periods of work.

23
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:27,964
Often, it’s run by other experienced volunteers as managers tend to prefer to get

24
00:01:27,964 --> 00:01:29,530
on with other things.

25
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:35,371
Now, I would ask you to consider a couple of important issues before you

26
00:01:35,371 --> 00:01:37,800
decide to apply for voluntary work.

27
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:42,736
We don’t worry about why you want to be a volunteer – people have

28
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:49,296
many different reasons that range from getting work experience to just doing something they’ve

29
00:01:49,296 --> 00:01:50,420
always wanted to do.

30
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:55,151
But it is critical that you have enough hours in the day for whatever

31
00:01:55,151 --> 00:02:00,022
role we agree is suitable for you – if being a volunteer becomes stressful

32
00:02:00,022 --> 00:02:03,710
then it’s best not to do it at all.

33
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,546
You may think that your income is important,

34
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:08,920
but we don’t ask about that.

35
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:12,930
It’s up to you to decide if you can work without earning money.

36
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:16,040
What we value is dedication.

37
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:20,033
Some of our most loyal volunteers earn very little themselves

38
00:02:20,033 --> 00:02:25,050
but still give their full energy to the work they do with us.

39
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:26,093
OK,

40
00:02:26,093 --> 00:02:31,250
so let’s take a look at some of the work areas that we need volunteers for

41
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:34,180
and the sort of things that would help you in those.

42
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:37,370
You may wish simply to help us raise money.

43
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:41,158
If you have the creativity to come up with an imaginative

44
00:02:41,158 --> 00:02:47,691
or novel way of fundraising, we’d be delighted, as standing in the local streets

45
00:02:47,691 --> 00:02:52,220
or shops with a collection box can be rather boring!

46
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:57,076
One outdoor activity that we need volunteers for is litter collection

47
00:02:57,076 --> 00:03:04,180
and for this it’s useful if you can walk for long periods, sometimes

48
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:04,230
uphill.

49
00:03:04,230 --> 00:03:07,292
Some of our regular collectors are quite elderly,

50
00:03:07,292 --> 00:03:11,970
but very active and keen to protect the environment.

51
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:17,314
If you enjoy working with children, we have three vacancies for what are called

52
00:03:17,314 --> 00:03:18,780
‘playmates’.

53
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:26,040
These volunteers help children learn about staying healthy through a range of out-of-school activities.

54
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:29,270
You don’t need to have children yourself,

55
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:32,882
but it’s good if you know something about nutrition

56
00:03:32,882 --> 00:03:35,430
and can give clear instructions.

57
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:40,671
If that doesn’t appeal to you, maybe you would be interested in helping out

58
00:03:40,671 --> 00:03:45,270
at our story club for disabled children, especially if you have done some acting.

59
00:03:45,270 --> 00:03:50,629
We put on three performances a year based on books they have read

60
00:03:50,629 --> 00:03:56,310
and we’re always looking for support with the theatrical side of this.

61
00:03:56,310 --> 00:04:00,107
The last area I’ll mention today is first aid.

62
00:04:00,107 --> 00:04:05,422
Volunteers who join this group can end up teaching others in vulnerable groups who

63
00:04:05,422 --> 00:04:07,700
may be at risk of injury.

64
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:13,562
Initially, though, your priority will be to take in a lot of information

65
00:04:13,562 --> 00:04:17,170
and not forget any important steps or details.

66
00:04:17,170 --> 00:04:17,220
Right,

67
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:21,050
so does anyone have any questions …
